        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Sojourner Truth, Sacajawea, Eleanor of Aquitaine, Empress Theodora, Virginia Woolf, Susan B. Anthony, Georgia O'Keeffe, Barbe de Verrue, Judy Chicago\n- Works: The Dinner Party\n- Roles: abolitionist, women's rights activist\n\nFacts:\n- Sojourner Truth was born Isabella (Belle) Baumfree around 1797 and died on November 26, 1883.\n- Sojourner Truth was an African-American abolitionist and women's rights activist.\n- Judy Chicago created \"The Dinner Party.\"\n- \"The Dinner Party\" includes guests such as Sacajawea, Sojourner Truth, Eleanor of Aquitaine, Empress Theodora of Byzantium, Virginia Woolf, Susan B. Anthony, and Georgia O'Keeffe.\n- Barbe de Verrue is memorialized as a figure in \"The Dinner Party\" by Judy Chicago.",
